=begin
  dreavening_weapon.lic

  During a Dreavening, keeps your weapon in your right (main) hand so it gets blessed.

  Why: Dreaven's blessing goes to the weapon in your main hand ("Your weapon has been
  blessed. If you have another weapon you want blessed be sure to move it to your main
  hand now."). The ;dreavening script's eat_that_bread routine does `stow right` to free
  the hand for the manna bread / tart, `get`s the food and `gob`s it -- and never puts the
  weapon back (10/25: `[dreavening]>stow right` at 15:09:14 stowed the runestaff, then
  `get tart` / `gob my tart`). So after eating, your hands are empty when the blessing
  comes round.

  What it does: only while a Dreavening is on -- Dreaven is in the room with you and spoke
  in the room in the last 10 minutes, and it isn't within 30 minutes of "THIS DREAVENING IS
  FINISHED" -- if your right hand has been empty for 3 seconds in a row -- long enough that ;dreavening has
  finished eating, since it is holding food the whole time it's eating -- it does `ready
  weapon`. If the weapon is in your LEFT hand and the right is empty, it does `swap`.
  Outside a Dreavening it does nothing at all, so it won't interfere with scrolls, wands,
  instruments or anything else that has your hands.

  10/25: it readied the weapon two minutes after the Dreavening ended (and you had stowed
  it): Dreaven keeps posting [Dreavening] thoughts after FINISHED ("Top mana senders...",
  "Please remember ALL tips...") and before the next one ("Next Dreavening is in 5
  minutes"), and every one of them counted as "a Dreavening is on". Thoughts no longer count
  at all, only Dreaven speaking in your room, and FINISHED starts a lockout.

  Usage:
    ;dreavening_weapon            start it (stays running; ;kill dreavening_weapon stops it)
    ;autostart add --global dreavening_weapon     to start it with every character, like
                                                  ;dreavening itself

  It never touches dreavening.lic. Tunables (below) are methods, so an edit applies the
  next time the script starts.
=end

# seconds the right hand must stay empty before the weapon comes back out
def hold_secs; 3; end
# a Dreavening counts as "on" for this long after Dreaven last spoke in the room
def active_window; 600; end
# ...and not at all for this long after it FINISHED (the next one is hours away)
def finished_lockout; 1800; end

$dreavening_weapon_active_until = 0
$dreavening_weapon_locked_until = 0

DownstreamHook.add("dreavening_weapon", proc { |line|
  text = line.to_s.gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '')
  if text =~ /THIS DREAVENING IS FINISHED/i
    $dreavening_weapon_active_until = 0
    $dreavening_weapon_locked_until = Time.now.to_f + finished_lockout
  elsif text =~ /\bDreaven (?:says|exclaims|yells),/ && text !~ /GSIV:/ &&
        Time.now.to_f >= $dreavening_weapon_locked_until
    $dreavening_weapon_active_until = Time.now.to_f + active_window
  end
  line
})
before_dying { DownstreamHook.remove("dreavening_weapon") }

echo "dreavening_weapon: watching for a Dreavening; will keep your weapon in your main hand during one."

empty_since = nil
loop do
  sleep 1

  if Time.now.to_f >= $dreavening_weapon_active_until || dead? ||
     GameObj.pcs.none? { |pc| pc.noun == "Dreaven" }
    empty_since = nil
    next
  end

  if checkright
    empty_since = nil
    next
  end

  empty_since ||= Time.now.to_f
  next if Time.now.to_f - empty_since < hold_secs

  waitrt?
  if checkleft && GameObj.left_hand.type.to_s =~ /weapon/
    echo "dreavening_weapon: weapon is in your left hand -- swapping it to the main hand."
    fput "swap"
  else
    echo "dreavening_weapon: right hand is empty during the Dreavening -- readying your weapon."
    fput "ready weapon"
  end
  empty_since = nil
  sleep 5 # give it time to land before looking again
end
